<title>SWITZERLAND: SOCCER-BRAZIL STAY FIRMLY ON TOP OF WORLD GAME.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-BRAZIL STAY FIRMLY ON TOP OF WORLD GAME.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Newly-crowned South American</p>
<p>soccer champions Brazil have become the first team ever to notch</p>
<p>up more than 70 points in the world rankings.</p>
<p>In the latest edition issued by FIFA on Wednesday, the 1994</p>
<p>World Cup winners retain their top position with 71.85 points,</p>
<p>more than eight points ahead of nearest rivals Spain.</p>
<p>European champions Germany have lost ground slightly in</p>
<p>fifth behind Denmark and Romania in third and fourth places</p>
<p>respectively. The Germans' truimph at last year's European</p>
<p>championship in England no longer counts in full.</p>
<p>Eighth-placed England are just ranked ahead of their World</p>
<p>Cup qualifying group rivals Italy who are ninth.</p>
